WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.176
Make running the tests non-negotiable.

2
00:00:02.456 --> 00:00:06.317
There’s a ladder of strictness, and the best-practices page lays it out.

3
00:00:06.597 --> 00:00:14.149
At the bottom, ask in the prompt (“run the auth tests after, and keep going until they pass”); Claude decides when it’s satisfied.

4
00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:16.072
Put the test command in CLAUDE.

5
00:00:16.352 --> 00:00:18.144
md so it always knows how.

6
00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:22.456
Next, a goal condition that a separate model checks after each turn.

7
00:00:22.736 --> 00:00:34.128
At the top, a Stop hook: Claude Code runs your script whenever Claude tries to end its turn, and if the script exits with code 2, Claude is sent back to work with your stderr as the reason.

8
00:00:34.408 --> 00:00:40.424
That’s enforced by the harness, so the turn doesn’t end until the check passes or the block limit is reached.

9
00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:49.664
And independent of all of these, CI runs the suite on every pull request, because the last word should belong to something the agent doesn’t control.

10
00:00:49.944 --> 00:01:00.717
A PostToolUse hook that runs fast tests after each edit is a useful complement: failures land in the agent’s context immediately, while it still has the change in mind.

11
00:01:00.997 --> 00:01:04.155
Keep it fast, and leave the full suite for Stop and CI.
